* Methods continued

You can declare a method on non-struct types, too.

In this example we see a numeric type ⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000001⟫MyFloat⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000002⟫ with an ⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000003⟫Abs⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000004⟫ method.

You can only declare a method with a receiver whose type is defined in the same
package as the method.
You cannot declare a method with a receiver whose type is defined in another
package (which includes the built-in types such as ⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000005⟫int⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000006⟫).

⟪GTI18N_31c4fd0d_000007⟫

